meta {
  name: Create Interview Slot
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/interviews/slots
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffAccessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "mode": "gmeet",
    "scheduled_date": "2026-08-15",
    "start_time": "10:00",
    "end_time": "10:30",
    "interviewer_email": "interviewer@college.edu"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("interviewSlotId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Creates a fixed-time interview slot. `mode`: "gmeet" | "on_campus"
  ("telephonic" was removed entirely). Requires staff_member auth, no
  special permission code.

  409 ConflictError if the requested `mode` is currently disabled for this
  college — see Get Interview Settings / Update Interview Settings.

  For "gmeet": no meeting link input, and no link is created yet at this
  point either — `meetingUrl`/`meetingId` are `null` in this response.
  The Google Meet event (same Calendar/Meet integration used for
  counsellor session booking) is only created the first time a student
  actually books this slot (see Book Interview Slot, student-side) — a
  slot that never gets booked never gets a calendar event. Best-effort:
  if Google Meet isn't configured or the call fails at booking time, the
  link just stays `null`, same fallback behavior as counselling.

  `interviewer_email` — required when `mode` is "gmeet" (400
  ValidationError if missing), not used/not required for "on_campus".
  Added as an attendee on the Meet calendar event when it's created —
  this is what actually grants the interviewer access/an invite to the
  call. Independent of `interviewer_id` (a StaffMember reference, used
  only for display) — if both are set and the referenced staff member
  also has an email on file, both get added as attendees.

  For "on_campus": pass `campus_id` (must be one of this college's own
  Campus rows — 404 "Campus not found" otherwise) so the student-facing
  response carries the campus's structured address/city/state/pinCode/
  latitude/longitude. `venue` is an optional room/floor-level detail
  alongside it (e.g. "Room 3, Admin Block") — the Campus record itself
  doesn't capture that level of detail.

  `duration_mins` defaults to 30. No `max_capacity` input — every slot is
  a fixed 1-on-1 booking now, not admin-configurable.

  `start_time`/`end_time` are "HH:MM" 24-hour strings.

  400 ValidationError "Interview slots cannot be scheduled in the past" if
  scheduled_date + start_time combined is at or before the current time.
}
